{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>For to you and to your seed, etc.</b> The land of the Philistines is included within the granting of the Land, and with this the Ramban also agreed. And the verse's saying <b>to you</b> — this promise is perhaps concerning the success he had there, as it is written (Genesis 26:12): ״וַיִּזְרַע יִצְחָק בָּאָרֶץ הַהִיא״, etc. Further, it intends to say to him that he will merit through it to have seed. Or perhaps, since Abraham did not hold the land of the Philistines with a firm possession at first, therefore HaShem wanted Isaac to establish his hold in it, and he did establish his hold in it with an excellent possession, for he plowed and sowed — and therefore HaShem was precise in His words to him, saying: ״אֶת כָּל הָאֲרָצוֹת הָאֵל״." "<b>Further,</b> it intends to promise him that Ishmael has no portion or inheritance in the promises to Abraham, aside from Isaac alone — and that is the meaning of saying <b>to you.</b> And He was precise in saying <b>and to your seed</b> to exclude a portion to his sons, for only the one called his seed — as it is written (Genesis 21:12): ״כִּי בְיִצְחָק יִקָּרֵא לְךָ זָרַע״ (Nedarim 31a) — and not all of Isaac [sc. not all who descend from Isaac, but only Jacob]."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:43:30.180326562Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}